  :adr/body "## What moved

`cloud.itonami.app.vf-authority` (ADR-2609111230 slice 2) issues the biscuit
scopes `kotoba://vf/<org>/<plane>/<action>` that give workforce bots an
economic surface over the shared VF event journal. Most of the file is
mechanism the native word-typed slice deliberately refuses — keyword
conversion (`keyword` / `name`), wire-string assembly (`str`), the
capability→scope map, and every `authority.scope` call (`parse` / `meet` /
`covered?` in `attenuate-slices` and `authorized?`). All of that stays host.

What moved is the one thing in the file that is a DECISION about plain
strings: whether a (plane, action) pair exists in the ADR's admission table.

    event       read, append
    commitment  read, commit
    agreement   read
    resource    read

The cljc's `vf-scope` refused through a `planes` map
(`(when-let [acts (planes p)] (when (contains? acts a) ...))`), and every
other scope constructor routes through `vf-scope`. The table IS that
refusal, so the core expresses it on the native slice as a total function
of the two names, and the host prepares `(name p)` / `(name a)` and
assembles the wire string only on admission.

Landed this tick:

- `src/cloud/itonami/app/vf_authority_core.kotoba` — `scope-admitted?`,
  `:string :string` in, `:bool` out; the ADR's four planes written out as
  `or` / `and` / `string=?` limbs, no map
- `kotoba_oracle.cljc` `cores` gains `:vf-authority-core`
- `vf_authority.clj` `vf-scope` routes on the core verdict through
  `kotoba-oracle`; the `planes` map is gone (the core owns the table) and
  the keyword/name/str/scope machinery stays host
- parity test `test/cloud/itonami/app/vf_authority_kotoba_parity_test.cljk`
  + KIR regeneration + JVM-free gen_kir_amu identity

## The split is byte-faithful, not just behavior-preserving

The refusal is a total function of the two names, and the cljc's
`when-let`/`when` over the `planes` map IS this table. The core invents
nothing: a pair the ADR does not define answers false, so `vf-scope`
returns nil. The existing `vf_authority_test.clj` (wire shape, refusal,
capability mapping, grant order, attenuation, prefix-confusion class) now
runs through the oracle path and pins it.

Nil discipline (ADR-2609081000): a nil or foreign plane/action produces a
name the table does not admit, so the answer is false — never a throw and
never a guessed scope. A guessed scope is invented authority; the core
invents nothing.

## Measured bounds on the pinned verifier (amu bin, jvm-free)

- `amu check src/cloud/itonami/app/vf_authority_core.kotoba --jvm-free` →
  `:ok true, :effects #{}` (the authoritative gate; measured on the landed
  core)
- `or` / `and` / `string=?` with `:string` literals and a `:bool` result →
  admitted (the same shape ADR-2609081000 / ADR-2609081200 measured)
- `keyword` / `name` / `str` concatenation, maps, sets and the
  `authority.scope` calls do NOT cross the slice — that is why the host
  keeps them

## Status

Accepted. The 14-layer topo map (ADR-2609081000) lists `vf-authority` as
a layer-0 wave-0 candidate; measured 2026-09-08 by
